ed new map and one Tossup rating keep this from being rated any stronger than Likely Democratic.", "watch": "A late national environment shift or uneven turnout among South Texas Latino voters could narrow the margin enough to put the seat in play.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Vicente Gonzalez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Vicente Gonzalez, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in a South Texas district that Republicans redrew to lean their way by about three points. Republican challenger Eric Flores has run a well-funded campaign, but outside groups have spent heavily against him while Gonzalez holds a large cash advantage. Most race raters call the contest Lean Democratic, with two rating it Likely Democratic and one calling it a Tossup.\n\nThe most recent independent poll, from mid-October, showed Gonzalez ahead by seven points among likely voters, an improvement on narrower August margins. Betting markets price his chances near nine in ten. Headlines emphasize Latino voters' leftward drift and the possibility that the new map could backfire on Republicans, though a Trump rally in Texas underscores GOP mobilization efforts. The race leans Democratic but remains within reach for Flores if conditions shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7446, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8106, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7774, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7834, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7562, "margin": 4.0}, {